```

## Example 2 — Return only the match
```bash
awk -F "|" '{if ($1 == 13) print $1 "\t" $2 "\t" $3}' report.txt
```
No `else` branch here — only prints when the condition is true.
**Output:**
```
013     Invoice_10492_AcmeCorp.pdf      2026-09-10
```

## Example 3 — Pattern-action rule
```bash
awk -F "|" '$3 == "2026-09-12" { print $0}' report.txt
```
Condition sits outside `{}`, no `if` needed — same effect as filtering, shorter to write.
**Output:**
```
014|Product_Roadmap_2027.pptx|2026-09-12
```

## Example 4 — Ternary operator
```bash
awk -F "|" '{ print ( $1 ~ /^00/) ? $0 : "error"}' report.txt
```
One-line version of if/else: `condition ? value_if_true : value_if_false`.
**Output:**
```
